<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2369"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 1:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;There was no evidence of a struggle at the home, on K-254 just east of the Butler/Sedgwick county line. Asked if there was any sign of forced entry or robbery, Murphy said an item missing from the home was later found elsewhere and has become important. <BR> <BR>Douglas Mould, Carol Mould&#39;s husband, said the item had her name on it and had been in her purse.&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>That fact is interesting...maybe the kiiler took her DL or an ID card...and dropped it? <BR> <BR>B <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
