<!--Post: 3180--><!--Time: 1104556697-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3180"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 9:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would not surprise me in a bit if BTK is linked to several previous cold cases not only in the Wichita area, but elsewhere. So many unsolved atrocities, like: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.portlandonline.com/police/index.cfm?&amp;a=60304&amp;c=3587460304&amp;c=35874" target=_top>http://www.portlandonline.com/police/index.cfm?&amp;a= 60304&amp;c=3587460304&amp;c=35874</a> <BR> <BR>With this in mind, it would behoove those investigating to contact jurisdictions outside of Wichita to perhaps gain more insight into the movement of possible suspects. I think John Doulgas meant for this to truly happen with VICAP, but I am not sure how that has turned out in 2005.  <BR> <BR>It would also be advantageous to go ahead and realize that BTK is diverse in MO--obviously, even in Wichita, he did change it. In some of the known cases he used a fake ID to gain entrance, when in others, he waited in the dark until the victim came home.  <BR> <BR>I think it is also likely that his signature may have morphed over time--research doesn&#39;t support this, but to be fair, there aren&#39;t that may 30 year longitudal studies of serial killers. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3180-->
<!--Post: 3182--><!--Time: 1104563296-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3182"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 11:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A couple of other items referencing Douglas Mould <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.webs.wichita.edu/wcpip/AlumniList.html" target=_top>http://www.webs.wichita.edu/wcpip/AlumniList.html</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.google.ca/local?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;q=douglas%2Be%2Bmould&amp;near=Wichita%2C%2BKS&amp;oi=localr" target=_top>http://www.google.ca/local?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;q=douglas&#43;e&#43;m ould&amp;near=Wichita,&#43;KS&amp;oi=localr</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3182-->
<!--Post: 3195--><!--Time: 1104603738-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3195"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 10:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The last link: Wow... that&#39;s close! I wonder how high up the office is/ what floor? <BR> <BR>I mentioned this in the Profile part 2 threadL: <BR> <BR>One other erie thing that stood out in those links: Dr. Mould in writing about Womens violence against men:  <BR> <BR>This is not a new issue for me &#40;Mould, 1984a, 1986, 1987, 1990a, 1990b&#41;. In 1984 the local United Way ran an ad showing a woman in sunglasses with an obviously bruised cheek. The headline read &#34;Her Mr. Right had a powerful left...&#34;  <BR> <BR>Julie Otero is pictured wearing sunglasses and her cheek bone was broken but most often discribed as being bruised.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3195-->
<!--Post: 3197--><!--Time: 1104605877-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3197"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:s.glasscock@sbcglobal.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Questions<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Questions<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 10:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q- Are you thinking that Julie was a victim of abuse in her marriage?  Mould was Mr. Otero&#39;s &#34;Dr&#34;, and he took care of the problem for her?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3197-->
<!--Post: 3223--><!--Time: 1104637393-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3223"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 7:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No not at all. <BR> <BR>Does that make any sense and how you draw that from what I commented on is beyond me: &#40;mainly the plethora of info about Dr. Douglas E. Mould or Douglas Mould assuming they are all the same person&#41; <BR> <BR>There are some very interesting if not odd circunstances that cross ref each other. <BR> <BR>I have no conclusion about it. <BR> <BR>You seem to have drawn one that frankly makes little sense to me. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3223-->
<!--Post: 3274--><!--Time: 1104721106-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3274"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jabez<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jabez<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 6:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Power in its purest form is &#40;merely&#41; the ability to have impact on another, and can be covert as well as overt. When what one wants from another is deference, affirmation, or reciprocity, it is the other who holds the ultimate power. The man who wants most to be sexually desired by a woman is at her mercy even if it is he who can take her life.&#34;   <BR> <BR>This statement is taken from the above mentioned link <a href="http://www.ipt-forensics.com/journal/volume9/j9_3_3.htm" target=_top>http://www.ipt-forensics.com/journal/volume9/j9_3_ 3.htm</a>  <BR> <BR>An eerie statement given the fact it was written by someone who&#39;s wife is dead.  I don&#39;t know much about BTK, but I have looked into Dr. Douglas E. Mould-and yes, he and Douglas Mould are one in the same.  Dr. Mould is the son of an episcopal  priest also by the name of Doug Mould.  Father Doug Mould died in January of 1998.  Doug&#39;s mother, Doris, died two years earlier.  <BR> <BR> I have come across two books with the name of A PREACHERS SON...both, in their own ways, will spark your interest.  Book One is written by Carl Weber.  THe main character in this book is Bishop T.K. Wilson &#40;B.T.K&#41;.  Book Two is written by Lynn Chandler Willis.  THe book is based on a real life event that took place in North Carolina.  THe son of a preacher murdered his wife then left her body in the house to burn...Carol Mould was found burned.   <BR> <BR>Whether DR. Mould is BTK &#40;I don&#39;t believe he is&#41;-whether he is &#34;stealing&#34; some of BTK&#39;s characteristics to throw off the case or whether he just did it on his own creation and we are the ones bringing BTK in on it...if he isn&#39;t, I think he should be the #1 suspect in his wife&#39;s murder.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3274-->
<!--Post: 3276--><!--Time: 1104723264-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3276"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 7:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;I think he should be the #1 suspect in his wife&#39;s murder.&#34; <BR> <BR>That is one of the things bothering me about the case. Normally the spouse is the first suspect.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3276-->
